{"kind":"artifact","text":"CI suite dedup, repair head: spike/cmd/gitseq-report/main_test.go at 57f90c9f745983bb4e7f45f81e9e9727112e1cac on request/ci-suite-dedup-current. Self-initiated planner work under ratified direction 0fbed766, finding #4. This head answers codex's ratified changes-requested verdict 928bfcc1 on 479a12aa, whose single blocker was that GitHub runs the step under bash -e -o pipefail, so a failing go test aborted the step before make spike consumed the captured stream and a red run projected no adversarial evidence. The step now captures the suite status, projects once from the captured stream on both the passing and failing paths, and then returns that status; make build moved after the status check so it still runs only on green. No test runs twice. The ordering is pinned by a new rule in internal/ciguard, following that package's stated convention of decoding the workflow rather than matching text. Verified at this exact commit: go build and go vet clean, go test ./internal/ciguard/... -count=1 ok.","body":{"commit":"57f90c9f745983bb4e7f45f81e9e9727112e1cac","path":"spike/cmd/gitseq-report/main_test.go"}}